      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. My main worry is that even with a good framework, there's always that danger of \"rogue\" items—stuff that somehow slips through the cracks or gets shoved into the wrong place by mistake during a busy period. How does a librarian handle those little pockets of disorder that seem to pop up unexpectedly in a massive collection?",
