      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Librarians often refer to these slips as \"unclassified\" or \"temporarily misplaced\" items. A best practice is to have a well-maintained cataloging workflow and a robust search system in place. This will enable quick detection and recovery of items that have been misplaced. Regular inventory checks and tactile exams of shelves can also help identify rummaging attempts and restore items to their intended location.",
      "source": "target",
